<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gujarat</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gujarat is a region in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> with a long coastline and a history of maritime trade. It was brought under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a> in the course of its western campaigns. In the eighteenth century the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a> extended its authority and revenue claims into Gujarat during its expansion across India.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gujarat.jpg" alt="Gujarat" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gagnon · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rani_ki_vav_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
